{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "L"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 126, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual helps far more when it replaces a missing edge (13, 20-22: often +20 to +37) than when it replaces an existing conv or pool (17-19)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the 0->3 skip, deleting edge 0 starves nodes 1 and 2 and collapses accuracy (31, 32), while with the skip present the effect is small (23-29)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 1 is already absent, removing edge 0 disconnects the whole intermediate path (30, 31: down to -36 on CIFAR-10)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is missing, edge 5 is the only conv route into the output, so removing it is very damaging (64, 65) compared with the near-neutral cases."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on 1->3 partly stands in for the missing residual when edge 3 is none (82, 88, 90), but it is redundant or harmful when edge 3 is already a skip (81, 83-86)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping in a skip on 0->2 gives the cell a shortcut that is useful only when there is no direct residual (94 is positive on all three datasets; most others with e3=skip are negative)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "With e0 = skip, making e4 a skip creates a parameter-free 0->1->3 path in parallel with the 0->3 skip, so conv capacity is lost (84: -23 on CIFAR-100; 89)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In pooling-dominated cells the network has little learnable capacity, so adding a residual brings only small gains (15) compared with conv cells."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 5 is none, node 2 never reaches the output, so adding a conv on 0->2 brings no benefit and changes optimization (34, 36, 42 all show negative CIFAR-100 changes)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, the 0->1 edge feeds the only remaining conv path to the output (via edge 4), so removing it is catastrophic (32: -42 on CIFAR-10)."}], "tok": 17544, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv